### Étape 4 — Poser les Voters Symfony (`BookingVoter` & `TripVoter`)

Votre feuille de route prévoit de séparer **rôles techniques** (`ROLE_USER`, `ROLE_ADMIN`) et **rôles contextuels** via Voters. Créez ces deux Voters dès maintenant :

#### 1. `src/Security/Voter/BookingVoter.php`
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Security\Voter;

use App\Entity\Booking;
use App\Entity\User;
use App\Enum\BookingStatus;
use App\Enum\TripStatus;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Authentication\Token\TokenInterface;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Authorization\Voter\Voter;

final class BookingVoter extends Voter
{
    public const CANCEL_PASSENGER = 'BOOKING_CANCEL_PASSENGER';

    protected function supports(string $attribute, mixed $subject): bool
    {
        return $attribute === self::CANCEL_PASSENGER && $subject instanceof Booking;
    }

    protected function voteOnAttribute(string $attribute, mixed $subject, TokenInterface $token): bool
    {
        $user = $token->getUser();
        if (!$user instanceof User) {
            return false;
        }

        /** @var Booking $booking */
        $booking = $subject;
        $trip = $booking->getTrip();

        return $booking->getPassenger()?->getId() === $user->getId()
            && $booking->getStatus() === BookingStatus::CONFIRMED
            && $trip !== null
            && $trip->getStatus() === TripStatus::SCHEDULED;
    }
}
```

#### 2. `src/Security/Voter/TripVoter.php`
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Security\Voter;

use App\Entity\Trip;
use App\Entity\User;
use App\Enum\TripStatus;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Authentication\Token\TokenInterface;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Authorization\Voter\Voter;

final class TripVoter extends Voter
{
    public const BOOK = 'TRIP_BOOK';
    public const MANAGE = 'TRIP_MANAGE';
    public const CANCEL = 'TRIP_CANCEL';

    protected function supports(string $attribute, mixed $subject): bool
    {
        return in_array($attribute, [self::BOOK, self::MANAGE, self::CANCEL], true)
            && $subject instanceof Trip;
    }

    protected function voteOnAttribute(string $attribute, mixed $subject, TokenInterface $token): bool
    {
        $user = $token->getUser();
        if (!$user instanceof User) {
            return false;
        }

        /** @var Trip $trip */
        $trip = $subject;
        $isDriver = $trip->getDriver()?->getId() === $user->getId();

        return match ($attribute) {
            self::BOOK => !$isDriver && $trip->getStatus() === TripStatus::SCHEDULED,
            self::MANAGE => $isDriver,
            self::CANCEL => $isDriver && $trip->getStatus() === TripStatus::SCHEDULED,
            default => false,
        };
    }
}
```

